    <briefdescription>
<para><ref refid="franzi-gb_8cpp_a8818ff25e637ee7d384c122f52a46d62_1a8818ff25e637ee7d384c122f52a46d62" kindref="member">Pairs</ref> a <computeroutput><ref refid="structgbvector" kindref="compound">gbvector</ref></computeroutput> with its evolving syzygy <computeroutput><ref refid="structgbvector" kindref="compound">gbvector</ref></computeroutput>. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><computeroutput><ref refid="struct_p_o_l_y_a99d4e7b185b16968de58cb6c47ef605e_1a99d4e7b185b16968de58cb6c47ef605e" kindref="member">f</ref></computeroutput> is the polynomial in the current module and <computeroutput><ref refid="struct_p_o_l_y_a7efdb8993698f844b8afabb2f926eecd_1a7efdb8993698f844b8afabb2f926eecd" kindref="member">fsyz</ref></computeroutput> is the syzygy expressing how <computeroutput><ref refid="struct_p_o_l_y_a99d4e7b185b16968de58cb6c47ef605e_1a99d4e7b185b16968de58cb6c47ef605e" kindref="member">f</ref></computeroutput> was built from the original generators. Carried together throughout a Groebner basis computation so that the syzygy module can be reported alongside the basis. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
